nd a blockbuster, critically and commercially establishing Hill's independence. \"When Lauren Hill dropped her solo debut, The Miseducation of Lauren Hill, in 1998, she led off the album with the fierce lost ones, widely heard as a dis against her former bandmate from the Fuji's Wyclef Jean.\"","year":1998,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Here's The Beef Edition Part 2","url":"https://shows.acast.com/hit-parade/episodes/695d4ef8154465cd600c50df"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album made history by becoming the first hip-hop album to win Album of the Year, two years after Alanis Morissette's win. The album was described as being \"as much a singing album as a rapping album,\" highlighting the Grammy Academy's historical reticence towards pure rap music. \"a hip-hop album won album of the year for the first time when the miseducation of Lauren Hill went all the way.\"","year":1998,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"And the Grammy Goes to… Edition Part 2","url":"https://shows.acast.com/hit-parade/episodes/695d4eef154465cd600c4ddc"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Solo Debut Classic","body":"Lauryn Hill's solo debut album, released in 1998, began with the fierce track \"Lost Ones,\" which was \"widely heard as a diss against her former bandmate from the Fugees, Wyclef Jean.\" This album became a classic and a blockbuster, critically and commercially establishing Hill's independence. \"When Lauren Hill dropped her solo debut, The Miseducation of Lauren Hill, in 1998, she led off the album with the fierce lost ones, widely heard as a dis against her former bandmate from the Fuji's Wyclef Jean.\"","year":1998,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Here's The Beef Edition Part 2","url":null}]}],"book_tracks":[],"others":[{"id":125553835662134,"type":"song","name":"Doo Wop (That Thing)","year":1999,"weight":10},{"